# /etc/containers/systemd/vms-archive-retain.container — the archive resource
# has no controller; it has a policy, and this is the policy: repair, close
# event buckets, retain media and events by each camera's own days. Run by
# vms-archive-retain.timer, so the unit is oneshot and Restart is not set.
# ================================================================================================
# NOTES — what every part of this file does and why (kept beside the code, not in a separate document)
# ================================================================================================
# # vms-archive-retain.container — the archive resource's policy pass as a oneshot: repair, close buckets,
# retain media
#
# **Role.** The Quadlet unit at `/etc/containers/systemd/vms-archive-retain.container`, from which Quadlet
# generates `vms-archive-retain.service`. "The archive resource has no controller; it has a policy, and this
# is the policy": `python3 -m vms retain` runs `ArchiveResource.repair()`, `close_buckets(now)` and, per
# camera row, `retain(...)` by the camera's own days, then exits. It is started by `vms-archive-retain.timer`
# every ten minutes, so the unit is `Type=oneshot` and `Restart` is not set — a timer-driven pass restarts by
# the timer, not by systemd's restart logic. Checked by `tests/test_deploy_units.py` (`Type=oneshot`;
# `/data/platform` mounted `:ro,z`).
#
# ## Stanza by stanza
#
# ### `[Unit]`
# - `Description=VMS archive resource — the policy pass`
#
# ### `[Container]`
# - `Image=localhost/vmsserver:latest`
# - `Exec=python3 -m vms retain` — the `retain` verb of `vms/__main__.py`: repair, close buckets, media
#   retention per camera row (the VMS's), then the platform `Resource.retain()` for the event buckets by
#   `vms/retention/<cam>` (see `vms/__main__.py`).
# - `EnvironmentFile=/data/config/vms.env` — `PLATFORM_DIR` (to read the camera rows), `SPOOL`, `ARCHIVE`.
# - `Volume=/data/platform:/data/platform:ro,z` — read-only: "the policy reads rows, never writes them".
#   `retain` opens `FileVariables` with no writer and only calls `list` and `get` (the camera rows, and
#   `vms/retention/<cam>` through the platform's `retention_days`); the mount enforces the same thing in
#   bytes. The `Resource` it builds writes no heartbeat here — the object store is opened but only the
#   retention policy runs.
# - `Volume=/data/spool:/data/spool:z` — read-write, though the `retain` verb only constructs the
#   `ArchiveResource` (which `makedirs` the root) and does not touch spool files; `repair` and `retain` work
#   under the archive.
# - `Volume=/data/archive:/data/archive:z` — read-write: `repair` rewrites manifests, `close_buckets` appends
#   bucket lines, `retain` deletes expired media files and rewrites the manifest.
#
# ### `[Service]`
# - `Type=oneshot` — the process runs once and exits; the service is "active" only while it runs, and
#   `OnUnitActiveSec` in the timer counts from that activation.
#
# ### `[Install]`
# None: the timer is what gets enabled; the service is pulled in by `Unit=` in the timer.
#
# ## Notes
# - Idempotent by construction: `repair` returns `{0, 0}` on a clean tree, `close_buckets` `[]` when
#   everything is indexed, `retain` `0` when nothing is past its cutoff — running the pass twice changes
#   nothing (`test_manifest_rebuilt_from_the_files_alone`,
#   `test_events_are_buckets_on_the_resource_recording_or_not`).
# - In М11 the same steps become `ArchivePolicy.pass_` registered on the platform's `Resource` job and run on
#   its timer beside bucket retention and the mirror.
# ================================================================================================
[Unit]
Description=VMS archive resource — the policy pass

[Container]
Image=localhost/vmsserver:latest
Exec=python3 -m vms retain
EnvironmentFile=/data/config/vms.env
Volume=/data/platform:/data/platform:ro,z
Volume=/data/spool:/data/spool:z
Volume=/data/archive:/data/archive:z

[Service]
Type=oneshot
